WEBVTT

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.480
<b>Year 1415
France - Paris</b>

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.360
Citizens!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.030
Harfleur has fallen, but do not fear!

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.580
France is blessed with 
God's divine protection!

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.250
The day we repel the English army

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.920
and put an end to this 
prolonged war is near!

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.840
<b>#01 Alchemy and Fairies</b>

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.390
Who's there? You can't just walk in here!

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.390
Sorry, but the store's not open yet!

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.230
And just when are you going to be open?

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.730
Oh, it's just you again.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.400
I don't have new grimoires in yet.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.110
Don't you get sick of coming here 
looking for those every day?

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.780
What's that?

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.200
Whoa!

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:01.490
Hmph. That's not a book you could read.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.330
Put it on my tab!

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.420
For crying out loud...

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.670
Thanks, Master!

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.880
I'm not your master!

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.430
The Beast of the Apocalypse, eh?

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.770
Our nation has been under 
invasion by our neighbor,

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.190
England, since the last century.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:34.360
The two nations have been at war 
since the year I was born.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.610
That's nearly eighty years now.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:43.740
One day, historians will refer to this 
conflict as the "Hundred Years' War."

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:48.040
This war between two Christian nations

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.290
for the rule of the kingdom has resulted 
in bloodshed and devastated earth,

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:56.880
creating much hardship for the peoples 
of both France and England.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.720
Good grief.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.770
Ow!

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.530
Guess that's as far as 
I can get on my own...

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.070
Montmorency.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.830
Oh... Richemont!

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.330
Can't you knock?

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.580
You left the door open.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.210
You have the lowest marks in 
the class in the military arts,

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.800
martial arts, and equestrian arts.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:39.050
On top of that, your poor attendance 
puts you at risk of failing.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.720
And this heresy you study...

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:42.760
It's not heresy!

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.510
Call it "alchemy"!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.690
Montmorency!

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.770
Richemont must have gotten here first.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.150
I-I'm sorry!

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:58.860
Hmph!

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.530
Ah, um...

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.450
I-Is Montmorency...

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.870
Bah! Why is a guy like him so popular?

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.580
Transmutation with the Philosopher's Stone!

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.830
This is the ultimate secret art!

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.960
They say the Stone turns 
its owner immortal!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.880
Which means, if we master alchemy—

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.350
If we master alchemy,

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.600
no one will have to die in battle anymore.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.940
No reaction?

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.360
I've heard this a hundred times.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.950
So you want to buy up all the 
grimoires you can find...

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.160
That's just it!

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.780
I've read a bunch, and it's 
like they're written in code!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.990
I'm not gonna get anywhere unless 
I get that old man to teach me!

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.870
Nicolas Flamel...

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.040
The alchemist rumored to have learned 
the secret art of Kabbalah.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.210
I don't know what rumors you've heard, 
but I'm just an old bookseller.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.760
Ask someone else.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.720
Who does he think he's fooling?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.760
Are you done talking now?

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.890
Then let's talk about reality.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:12.770
Our nation has already let 
the English army come in

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.810
and take control of Harfleur.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:19.820
As a noble, it's your duty to become 
a knight and end this war.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:24.110
I'd rather have a job that saves 
lives than one that takes them.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.870
Montmorency...

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:29.620
Oh, yeah!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.330
Are you free tonight?

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.000
Huh?

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.970
What am I doing, exactly?

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.560
Hold it!

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.440
Charlotte?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.690
Philip?

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.360
Fairies?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.200
Yeah! I saw them, plain as day!

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.420
Hey, were those—

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.680
As you know, fairies are seen 
as retainers of demons

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.300
and are hunted down by the church.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:32.010
So why does Nicolas Flamel 
keep a bunch of them?

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:36.190
Fairies must be connected 
to alchemy somehow!

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.190
Alchemy...

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.900
If the old man won't teach it to me,

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.490
I'll just have to ask the fairies.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.070
It could at least help me start to understand.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.490
F-Fairies don't bite, do they?

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:55.330
I once heard of someone who had 
a finger bitten off by a fairy.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.870
Cut it out, Charlotte.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:03.750
One might have even gone in through 
someone's mouth and eaten their innards...

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.050
Charlotte...

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:06.720
Hmph!

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.470
Quiet. The fairies will run away.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.970
Why are you only ever nice to Philip?

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.100
Because you're always causing trouble—

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.570
I have a little sister, so I'm used 
to this. Don't worry about it.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:35.990
Sorry.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.080
He's not just nice to Philip.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.580
He's nice to everyone.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.710
That's why it makes me so mad.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:49.010
Montmorency!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.140
What is it?!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.140
Th-They're...

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.020
English soldiers!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.020
What?!

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:04.190
Richemont!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.820
Your fight is with m—

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.660
He's weak!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.030
A-Are you okay?

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.580
I'm... fine...

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:22.330
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:33.840
Take this!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.890
You did it! What was that?

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.060
Pepper and ash.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.230
It's not even poison?!

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.690
I can't make anything that dangerous!

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.100
Oh, honestly!

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:45.980
Play along.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:46.610
Huh?

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.480
You'd best turn back!

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.530
Do you know who this man is?

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.870
He is the first pupil of the 
famous Nicolas Flamel,

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.410
The Alchemist of Black Death, Montmorency!

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.040
The one and only!

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.960
That's right!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:05.080
And my next trick will be 
to turn a man to stone!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:09.550
Sorry, though. My master hasn't taught 
me how to turn them back yet!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.300
<i>I have to buy time until Richemont 
takes that guy out...</i>

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.930
Ph-Philosopher's Stone!

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.810
By your limitless magical power,

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.850
turn this mortal into an 
invincible berserker!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.920
Let's die here together, shall we?

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:08.520
I didn't realize the English had 
made it this far into France.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:11.320
There. You should be fine now.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.570
It's not like our mock battles.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:19.870
Be proud!

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.160
You're strong, Richemont!

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.500
Montmorency...

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.330
We won because of my strategy!

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.590
Yes, I know. Great job.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:33.670
I-I'm pretty sure I played 
a significant role, too...

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:37.720
You guys should be praising my 
Philosopher's Stone too, then!

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.470
It's just a rock.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:45.310
This stone was buried deep 
in my family's storehouse.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:48.350
There are piles of ancient 
treasures in there!

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.320
I think it's just a rock.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.320
You don't have to be so blunt about it!

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.490
I wish things could stay like this forever.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.780
We all study side by side,

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:04.290
but I am of the noble house of Brittany,

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.870
Charlotte is of the French royal family,

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.960
and Philip is of the house of Burgundy.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:12.500
We live in mad times.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.010
We may one day face each other 
as political opponents,

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.890
or even fight on opposing 
sides of the battlefield.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.350
But if possible,

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.310
I would love it if we could 
stay friends forever.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:32.730
We can, if that's what we want.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:35.400
We're the strongest team around!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.900
We can do anything!

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.150
We even beat up English soldiers.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:39.990
Yeah, that's ri—

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.070
Curse all you French bastards!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:42.990
Shut up!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:44.870
The stone!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:45.950
Oh, crap!

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.840
Hey, why don't we swear an oath?

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.550
To stay friends forever.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.100
Let's do it, then!

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.100
We will...

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.350
We will...

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.770
...even after we graduate from school...

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.230
...remain best friends forever!

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:49.140
Please try to remember 
the position you're in.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:54.440
You are a noble lady in line 
to succeed the throne.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.900
I have two older brothers.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:59.690
I won't be succeeding the throne.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.280
Then you should have taken me with you!

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.530
I am your attendant.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:07.120
It's my duty to put my life 
on the line for you.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.250
Oh? How very manly of you.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:11.160
Yes!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.920
As of tomorrow, you'll wear 
women's underwear, too.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.210
Are we clear?

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.670
What?!

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:20.670
Honestly...

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:24.680
Just because I'm already overflowing 
with womanly appeal in my childhood...

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:27.600
All men are just wild animals in heat!

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.100
That's not what I meant...

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.100
A duel!

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.270
All you're doing is darting around.

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:38.520
And you call yourself a knight 
in training, Montmorency?!

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:41.070
I challenge you to a duel!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.150
Why do we have to duel?

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:46.490
You put my Philip in danger 
out there in the forest!

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.450
She's not yours.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:49.080
Wrong!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:53.250
No man is a true knight until 
he swears his love to a lady.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:56.880
I've made up my mind to devote 
all my love to Philip!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.210
You heard Alençon.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.300
What do you think?

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.180
I-I'm sorry, but I must decline.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.340
Can I go now?

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.800
B-Blast you!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.470
That's enough, Alençon.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:11.470
Sister!

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:14.020
I went into the forest with them.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.810
You want a duel with me, too?

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:19.020
N-No, I wouldn't do something 
that dastardly...

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:22.110
Honestly... What does a child 
like you know about the love

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.740
between a man and a woman, anyway?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.450
I do know!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.450
I've read erotic books, too— Oh, crap!

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:34.270
Alençon, this is clearly a 
result of my own negligence.

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:38.970
I'll need to harden my heart and provide 
you with some tough discipline.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.920
W-Wait, Sister!

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.180
We need to talk.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:57.480
I received word from my brother

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.020
that the English troops at Harfleur 
have been stricken by an epidemic

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.650
and intend to retreat to Calais.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:07.780
The French army will lie in wait at 
Azincourt to initiate the decisive battle.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.280
I see.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.450
I'm leaving for Azincourt tomorrow.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:20.000
I'm joining the battle as a representative 
of the household of Brittany.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.590
But why you?!

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:24.420
Because my brother despises 
the battlefield.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.970
By sending me, my family can save face.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.340
I'll go, too!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.850
Wh-What?

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:37.680
I remain undefeated in 
the knight tournament,

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.900
and you've lost every round.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.390
Hey, come on!

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:43.610
Just because you're slightly strong, smart,

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:47.070
come from a noble bloodline, 
and were born with a pretty face

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:51.030
doesn't mean you can talk to a failure 
like me with pity in your eyes!

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:55.080
I'm glad I got to talk to you.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.910
I know this blazing sunset

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:02.250
will become one of the most 
beautiful memories in my life.

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:14.010
You want to use the Philosopher's Stone 
to make your childhood friend immortal?

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.560
There's not much time! 
Please! I'm begging you!

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.480
If one becomes something more than human,

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:26.400
one will be banished from 
the church as a heretic.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:27.230
Still...

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:31.320
Immortality means running away for eternity

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.030
and living alone for eternity.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:40.790
Then I'll—

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.330
I'm just an old bookseller.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.880
Ask someone else.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.720
Montmorency...

00:15:56.050 --> 00:16:00.850
I had hoped that you would remain a 
blockhead until your dying day, but...

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:06.860
Fight against fate, Beast of the Apocalypse.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:16.870
Brother!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.030
Coming?

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.040
Yes!

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:26.080
The French knights will mock us, 
saying we sold our souls to the devil.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:27.670
Even down in Hell.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.420
There is no Hell.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.380
That's just the rambling of the priests.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:36.300
In my world, there is only the realm 
of Earth and the realm of Heaven.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:40.220
Now, let us give them the finest 
hospitality we have to offer.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.110
Damn you!

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:53.240
What Catholic monarch would bear 
the heretics' crest of the devil?!

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.490
Henry V!

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:02.870
God, if you truly exist, I beseech you!

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:12.590
Please... Save Richemont!

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.830
Richemont!

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.150
Welcome back.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.360
Father...

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.860
There is nothing to fear.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:20.530
We've already made all the preparations 
to join forces with the English army.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:36.670
The only way to rescue Richemont, 
now that England's taken her,

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:39.760
is to become immortal myself!

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:46.770
If there is no God, 
then I'll sell my soul to the devil.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:57.320
If you are a relic of a civilization that 
fell before Christianity existed...

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.570
If you are a product of alchemy...

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.910
Please, guide me!

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.990
I offer you my soul in return!

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.730
I am Astaroth,

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:35.860
queen of the fairies.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.400
Was it...

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:42.530
Was it you who woke me from my slumber?

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:47.290
The queen of the fairies will 
never be kept by a human,

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.540
no matter how bad things are.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.540
So you will be my servant—

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.330
Fine.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.040
You accepted without hesitation...

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.670
I want the power to protect lives.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:01.170
After I prayed for that, you appeared,

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:05.300
as if someone were ordering 
me to be that protector.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:10.430
Very well. I will grant your wish.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:13.230
I am the guardian of the 
Philosopher's Stone, after all.

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.650
If you swallow the Philosopher's Stone,

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:17.860
its immense power will be yours.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:22.360
King Solomon, Clovis I, Otto the Great,

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.490
and Jesus Christ...

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:27.280
They all achieved great works 
through the power of the Stone,

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:28.950
earning them the title of "Ulysses."

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:32.210
Wait! Where is the 
Philosopher's Stone, anyway?

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.120
You truly are a fool.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:34.960
That's it.

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.840
One of your ancestors must have been 
a member of the Knights Templar.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:43.630
Their true goal was not to reclaim 
the holy land of Jerusalem.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.890
It was to find the Philosopher's 
Stone that lay there.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:55.310
But, Montmorency, do be careful.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.020
If you swallow the 
Philosopher's Stone as is,

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:01.360
it will turn into poison and kill you.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:07.570
You must first transmute it into a 
special liquid called the "Elixir."

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:13.080
Once you drink it, your body will 
be able to withstand the poison.

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:25.840
Damn it!

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.970
This just isn't working.

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.100
You have no talent.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:32.640
Shut up!

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.350
How long has it been?

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:38.560
Seven years.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.020
Huh?

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:49.950
<b>To be continued</b>

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:13.490
<b>Jeanne d'Arc and
the Alchemist Knight</b>

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:34.920
<b>#02 The Girl Called Jeanne</b>

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.060
Small breasts are dangerous!

00:23:22.060 --> 00:23:24.020
Should you fall for their 
appeal, you're done for!

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:25.730
It's straight to effeminate 
boys from there!

00:23:25.730 --> 00:23:27.820
You aren't the sort of 
perverts who'd lust after

00:23:27.820 --> 00:23:29.940
the smooth trunks of 
little girls, are you?!

00:23:29.940 --> 00:23:32.490
Episode 2: "The Girl Called Jeanne."

00:23:32.490 --> 00:23:34.320
You'll all be fine, right? Right?!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:44.940
<b>Surprisingly useful French lesson</b>

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:44.940
<b>"Like an animal during mating season!"</b>

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:44.940
<b>Use it when someone gives you a leering look!</b>
